\tag{lie}

\title{Differentiating and integrating Spin representations}

\p{The quadratic Clifford construction in the preceding section is
algebraic. A different bridge starts from a smooth homomorphism of Lie groups
and differentiates it at the identity. The concrete Spin calculation identifies
this differential with the normalized quadratic lift. For compact
#{\Spin(n)}, #{n\geq3}, simple connectedness then gives the reverse
construction: integration of a Lie-algebra representation. Its action on the
covering kernel decides whether it also represents #{SO(n)}.}

